      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"MATH-517: Assignment 3\"\n",
        "author: \"Nikita Gupta\"\n",
        "date: '05 October 2025'\n",
        "format: pdf\n",
        "editor: visual\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Theoretical exercise\n",
        "\n",
        "Your answer goes here\n",
        "\n",
        "## Practical exercise\n",
        "\n",
        "The goal of this simulation study is to see how changing parameters such as sample size $(n)$ , number of blocks $(N)$, and the $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ values for the underlying beta distribution for the covariate $X$, impacts the optimal bandwidth $h_{AMISE}$ . We do this for a regression function $Y=m(X) + \\epsilon$ where $m(X) = sin ((\\frac{x}{3}+0.1)^{-1})$ and $\\epsilon$ \\~ $N(0,\\sigma^2)$. I set $\\sigma^2$ =1 for simplicity. I run a simulation 200 times, iterating through all the parameters (running through all combinations of $\\alpha, \\beta, n, N$ ), and plot the average CP Mallow's and $h_{AMISE}$ for each of the combinations.\n",
        "\n",
        "From the graphs, we can see that as the number of blocks $N$ increases, the optimal bandwidth $h_{AMISE}$ decreases. In general, it decreases sharply at first but begins to stabilize as $N$ continues to increase. This is because when there are fewer observations per block, a smaller bandwidth $h$ could results in overfitting. This is also why as sample size $n$ increases, $h_{AMISE}$ decreases - because more observations are available per block, we can use a smaller bandwidth without overfitting.\n",
        "\n",
        "$N$ should depend on $n$ because it is important to have enough observations for each block. If $n$ is too small and we choose too large of a $N$ then each block $N$ will have too few observations, and there will not be enough data to average out the impact of noise per block. There may be a risk of overfitting as the polynomial may be \"wigglier\" and overfit to noise. When $n$ is large, more blocks can be chosen as more observations are available to fit data on within each block. There are many methods to determine an optimal $N$ . One option is to find the value that minimizes Mallow's $C_p(N) = \\frac{RSS(N)}{\\frac{RSS(N_{\\max})}{n - 5 N_{\\max}}} - (n - 10 N)$ where $RSS(N) = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\sum_{j=1}^{N} \\left\\{ Y_i - \\hat{m}_j(X_i) \\right\\}^2 \\mathbf{1}_{X_i \\in X}$ and $N_{\\max} = \\max \\left\\{ \\min \\left( \\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{20} \\right\\rfloor, 5 \\right), 1 \\right\\}$. In this simulation, Mallow's $C_p$ is minimized for the minimum number of blocks (N=2).\n",
        "\n",
        "The Beta distribution parameters $(\\alpha, \\beta)$ controls the shape of the distribution for X. As seen in the second set of graphs below, when $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are significantly different, then the data is skewed. This means that observations cluster in some regions, but not in others - resulting in some blocks having fewer observations and reducing the reliability of the polynomials from those blocks.\n",
        "\n",
        "I have also included a Shiny App in another file (shiny_app.py) to experiment with the parameters of the simulation. This can be run from the terminal (shiny run shiny_app.py)."
      ],
      "id": "979ff7f3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "message": false
      },
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "#| warning: false\n",
        "\n",
        "# Your code goes here. \n",
        "# The `echo: false` option disables the printing of code (only output is displayed).\n",
        "# The programming language can be changed to Python or Julia\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "#Step 1: Import necessary libraries\n",
        "\n",
        "from shiny import App, ui, render, reactive\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import PolynomialFeatures\n",
        "from scipy.stats import beta\n",
        "import math\n",
        "\n",
        "np.random.seed(13)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "#Step 2: create regression function\n",
        "# Regression function: m(x)\n",
        "def m_func(x):\n",
        "    return np.sin(1 / (x/3 + 0.1))\n",
        "\n",
        "#Step 3: Create simulation dataset (covariate X from a beta distribution Beta (α ,β))\n",
        "def simulate_data(n, alpha, beta_param, sigma_squared):\n",
        "    X = beta.rvs(alpha, beta_param, size=n) #beta distribution to create covariate X\n",
        "    epsilon = np.random.normal(0, np.sqrt(sigma_squared), size=n) #noise (normal(0, sigma^2))\n",
        "    Y = m_func(X) + epsilon\n",
        "    return X, Y\n",
        "\n",
        "#Step 4: divide into n-blocks and fit polynomial regression in each block (to estimate m(x) locally in each block)\n",
        "#Returns a list of fitted models for each block\n",
        "#Use this to estimate theta22 and sigma^2\n",
        "def fit_polynomial_n_blocks(X, Y, N_blocks):\n",
        "    #get sample size and divide into N blocks\n",
        "    n = len(X) \n",
        "    indices = np.array_split(np.arange(n), N_blocks)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    #create list to store block models\n",
        "    block_models = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    #for each block fit a 4th degree polynomial regression\n",
        "    for idx in indices:\n",
        "        #get x and y values for the block\n",
        "        Xi = X[idx].reshape(-1, 1) #(sklearn needs 2D array for features)\n",
        "        Yi = Y[idx] \n",
        "        \n",
        "        #convert data into polynomial (degree 4) form - transforms data to [1,x,x^2,x^3,x^4] - so x=0.5 becomes [1,0.5,0.25,0.125,0.0625]\n",
        "        #need to manually transform X data to polynomial form before fitting linear regression using sklearn\n",
        "        polynomial_transform = PolynomialFeatures(degree=4) \n",
        "        Xi_polynomial_transform = polynomial_transform.fit_transform(Xi)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        #create linear regression model and fit to X, Y from the block\n",
        "        model = LinearRegression()\n",
        "        model.fit(Xi_polynomial_transform, Yi)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        #store this block's model\n",
        "        block_models.append((model, idx))\n",
        "    return block_models\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "#Step 5: Using the fitted models from each block, estimate theta22 and sigma^2\n",
        "\n",
        "# Estimate theta22 by using second derivative of fitted polynomial in each block\n",
        "def estimate_theta22(X, block_models):\n",
        "    n = len(X)\n",
        "    theta_hat_vals = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    #for each block model, calculate second derivative estimates and their sum of squares\n",
        "    for model, idx in block_models:\n",
        "\n",
        "        #Convert X to polynomial features (degree 4)\n",
        "        poly = PolynomialFeatures(degree=4)\n",
        "        Xi = X[idx].reshape(-1, 1)\n",
        "        Xi_poly = poly.fit_transform(Xi)\n",
        "\n",
        "        #Get coefficients of the fitted polynomial\n",
        "        coefs = model.coef_\n",
        "        b0 = model.intercept_  \n",
        "        b1 = coefs[1]\n",
        "        b2 = coefs[2]\n",
        "        b3 = coefs[3]\n",
        "        b4 = coefs[4]\n",
        "\n",
        "        #compute 2nd derivative estimate\n",
        "        Xi_vals = X[idx]\n",
        "        #because m(x) = b0 + b1*x + b2*x^2 + b3*x^3 + b4*x^4, m''(x) is below\n",
        "        m_func_2nd_deriv_est =(2 * b2) + (6 * b3 * Xi_vals) + (12 * b4 * Xi_vals**2)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        #theta = sum of squares of 2nd derivative estimates in this block\n",
        "        theta_hat_vals.append(np.sum(m_func_2nd_deriv_est**2))\n",
        "    \n",
        "    #average theta over all blocks\n",
        "    return np.sum(theta_hat_vals) / n\n",
        "\n",
        "# Estimate sigma^2 & associated rss\n",
        "def estimate_sigma_squared(X, Y, block_models):\n",
        "    n = len(X)\n",
        "    rss_total = 0\n",
        "\n",
        "    #for each block model, calculate residual sum of squares and sum them\n",
        "    for model, idx in block_models:\n",
        "        Xi = X[idx].reshape(-1, 1) #reshape to 2d for sklearn\n",
        "        Yi = Y[idx]\n",
        "\n",
        "        #Convert X to polynomial features (degree 4)\n",
        "        poly = PolynomialFeatures(degree=4)\n",
        "        Xi_poly = poly.fit_transform(Xi)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        #use the fitted model to predict Y values and calculate residuals\n",
        "        preds = model.predict(Xi_poly)\n",
        "        residuals = Yi - preds\n",
        "\n",
        "        #add this block's RSS to total RSS\n",
        "        rss_total += np.sum(residuals**2)\n",
        "\n",
        "    #estimate sigma^2\n",
        "    sigma_squared_hat = rss_total / (n - 5 * len(block_models))\n",
        "    return sigma_squared_hat, rss_total\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "#Step 6: Compute h_AMISE and Mallow's Cp\n",
        "# Compute h_AMISE\n",
        "def compute_h_amise(n, sigma_squared_hat, theta22_hat, supp_x=1):\n",
        "    return (35 * sigma_squared_hat * abs(supp_x) / theta22_hat)**(1/5) * n**(-1/5)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Compute Mallow's Cp\n",
        "def compute_mallows_cp(rss_N_blocks, rss_N_block_max, n, N_blocks, N_block_max):\n",
        "    cp = (rss_N_blocks / (rss_N_block_max / (n - 5 * N_block_max))) - (n - 10 * N_blocks)\n",
        "    return cp\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "#Step 7: Run simulations\n",
        "def run_simulation(n, N_blocks, alpha, beta_param, sigma_squared=1, num_times=200):\n",
        "    h_amise_list=[]\n",
        "    cp_list=[]\n",
        "    for i in range(num_times):\n",
        "        X, Y = simulate_data(n, alpha, beta_param, sigma_squared) #create data\n",
        "        block_models = fit_polynomial_n_blocks(X, Y, N_blocks) #Fit polynomial models on N blocks\n",
        "        \n",
        "        #estimate theta22 and sigma^2\n",
        "        theta22_hat = estimate_theta22(X, block_models) \n",
        "        sigma_squared_hat, rss_N_blocks = estimate_sigma_squared(X, Y, block_models)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        #compute h_AMISE\n",
        "        h_amise = compute_h_amise(n, sigma_squared_hat, theta22_hat)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Compute mallow's cp  \n",
        "        N_block_max = max(min(n // 20, 5), 1) #compute n-max ( Ruppert et al. (1995) )\n",
        "        block_models_Nmax = fit_polynomial_n_blocks(X, Y, N_block_max) #fit polynomial models on Nmax blocks\n",
        "        sigma_squared_max, rss_N_block_max = estimate_sigma_squared(X, Y, block_models_Nmax) #get rss of n block max\n",
        "        cp = compute_mallows_cp(rss_N_blocks, rss_N_block_max, n, N_blocks, N_block_max) #compute CP\n",
        "\n",
        "        h_amise_list.append(h_amise)\n",
        "        cp_list.append(cp)\n",
        "    h_amise= np.sum(h_amise_list)/num_times\n",
        "    cp= np.sum(cp_list)/num_times\n",
        "    return h_amise, cp\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "sample_sizes = [100, 300, 500]\n",
        "block_sizes = [2, 4, 6, 8, 10]\n",
        "alphas = [2, 5, 10]\n",
        "betas = [2, 5, 10] #alpha big beta small issues\n",
        "\n",
        "#create empty list to store results\n",
        "results = []\n",
        "# Run simulations for different parameter combinations (by sample size, block size, alphas, and betas)\n",
        "for n in sample_sizes:\n",
        "    for N_blocks in block_sizes:\n",
        "        for alpha in alphas:\n",
        "            for beta_param in betas:\n",
        "                h_amise, cp = run_simulation(n, N_blocks, alpha, beta_param)\n",
        "                results.append({\n",
        "                    \"n\": n,\n",
        "                    \"N_blocks\": N_blocks,\n",
        "                    \"alpha\": alpha,\n",
        "                    \"beta\": beta_param,\n",
        "                    \"h_AMISE\": h_amise,\n",
        "                    \"Cp\": cp\n",
        "                })\n",
        "\n",
        "# Convert results to DataFrame\n",
        "df = pd.DataFrame(results)\n",
        "sns.set(style=\"whitegrid\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Set up the figure with subplots: sample_sizes × 2 (h_AMISE, Cp)\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(\n",
        "    nrows=len(sample_sizes),\n",
        "    ncols=2,\n",
        "    figsize=(12, 5 * len(sample_sizes)),\n",
        "    sharex=True,\n",
        "    sharey='col'  # Share y-axis within each column (h_AMISE, Cp)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Define colors and line styles to ensure consistency\n",
        "palette = sns.color_palette(\"tab10\", n_colors=len(alphas))\n",
        "linestyles = ['solid', 'dashed', 'dotted', 'dashdot']\n",
        "\n",
        "legend_handles = []\n",
        "legend_labels = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for i, n_val in enumerate(sample_sizes):\n",
        "    df_subset = df[df[\"n\"] == n_val]\n",
        "\n",
        "    # --- Plot h_AMISE (left column) ---\n",
        "    ax1 = axes[i, 0]\n",
        "    sns.lineplot(\n",
        "        data=df_subset,\n",
        "        x=\"N_blocks\", y=\"h_AMISE\",\n",
        "        hue=\"alpha\", style=\"beta\",\n",
        "        palette=palette,\n",
        "        ax=ax1,\n",
        "        markers=True,\n",
        "        dashes=True,\n",
        "        legend=False  # No individual legends here\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    ax1.set_title(f\"Sample Size: {n_val} — h_AMISE\")\n",
        "    ax1.set_xlabel(\"N_blocks\")\n",
        "    ax1.set_ylabel(\"h_AMISE\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    # --- Plot Cp (right column) ---\n",
        "    ax2 = axes[i, 1]\n",
        "\n",
        "    legend_flag = (i == len(sample_sizes) - 1)  # Legend only on last row\n",
        "\n",
        "    sns.lineplot(\n",
        "        data=df_subset,\n",
        "        x=\"N_blocks\", y=\"Cp\",\n",
        "        hue=\"alpha\", style=\"beta\",\n",
        "        palette=palette,\n",
        "        ax=ax2,\n",
        "        markers=True,\n",
        "        dashes=True,\n",
        "        legend=legend_flag\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    ax2.set_title(f\"Sample Size: {n_val} — Mallow's Cp\")\n",
        "    ax2.set_xlabel(\"N_blocks\")\n",
        "    ax2.set_ylabel(\"Cp\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    if legend_flag:\n",
        "        handles, labels = ax2.get_legend_handles_labels()\n",
        "        legend_handles = handles\n",
        "        legend_labels = labels\n",
        "\n",
        "# Place shared legend below all subplots\n",
        "fig.legend(\n",
        "    handles=legend_handles,\n",
        "    labels=legend_labels,\n",
        "    title=\"Alpha (color) / Beta (style)\",\n",
        "    loc='lower center',\n",
        "    bbox_to_anchor=(0.5, -0.02),\n",
        "    ncol=4,\n",
        "    frameon=False\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout(rect=[0, 0.05, 1, 0.95])\n",
        "plt.suptitle(\"Effect of Block Size N on h_AMISE and Mallow's Cp\", fontsize=18)\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "#only do 1 sample size - too many graphs otherwise.\n",
        "def plot_density_with_blocks_varying_params_grid(sample_size, alphas, betas, N_blocks=5, sigma_squared=1):\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Total number of plots\n",
        "    total_plots = len(sample_sizes) * len(alphas) * len(betas)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Define number of columns and rows\n",
        "    ncols = 3\n",
        "    nrows = math.ceil(total_plots / ncols)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    fig, axes = plt.subplots(nrows=nrows, ncols=ncols, figsize=(30, 4 * nrows), sharex=True, sharey=True)\n",
        "    axes = axes.flatten()  # flatten to 1D for easier indexing\n",
        "    \n",
        "    plot_idx = 0\n",
        "    \n",
        "    for n in sample_sizes:\n",
        "        for alpha in alphas:\n",
        "            for beta_param in betas:\n",
        "                ax = axes[plot_idx]\n",
        "                \n",
        "                # Simulate data\n",
        "                X, Y = simulate_data(n, alpha, beta_param, sigma_squared)\n",
        "                block_edges = np.quantile(X, np.linspace(0, 1, N_blocks + 1))\n",
        "                \n",
        "                # Count observations per block\n",
        "                counts = []\n",
        "                for i in range(N_blocks):\n",
        "                    if i == N_blocks - 1:\n",
        "                        count = np.sum((X >= block_edges[i]) & (X <= block_edges[i + 1]))\n",
        "                    else:\n",
        "                        count = np.sum((X >= block_edges[i]) & (X < block_edges[i + 1]))\n",
        "                    counts.append(count)\n",
        "                \n",
        "                # Plot  on current axis\n",
        "                sns.kdeplot(X, fill=True, bw_adjust=0.5, color=\"skyblue\", ax=ax)\n",
        "                ax.set_title(f\"Alpha, Beta ({alpha}, {beta_param}), n={n}, Blocks={N_blocks}\")\n",
        "                ax.set_xlabel(\"X\")\n",
        "                ax.set_ylabel(\"Density\")\n",
        "                \n",
        "                # Overlay block boundaries and counts\n",
        "                ylim = ax.get_ylim()\n",
        "                for i, edge in enumerate(block_edges):\n",
        "                    ax.axvline(edge, color='red', linestyle='--', alpha=0.7)\n",
        "                    if i < N_blocks:\n",
        "                        mid = (block_edges[i] + block_edges[i + 1]) / 2\n",
        "                        ax.text(mid, ylim[1] * 0.8, f'n={counts[i]}', \n",
        "                                ha='center', color='black', fontsize=10)\n",
        "                \n",
        "                plot_idx += 1\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Remove empty subplots if any\n",
        "    for i in range(plot_idx, len(axes)):\n",
        "        fig.delaxes(axes[i])\n",
        "    \n",
        "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "    fig.subplots_adjust(top=0.9)  # give space for suptitle\n",
        "    plt.suptitle(\"Density of X with Beta Distributions and Block Boundaries\", fontsize=16, y=1.02)\n",
        "    plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "plot_density_with_blocks_varying_params_grid(sample_size=500, alphas=alphas, betas=betas, N_blocks=5)\n"
      ],
      "id": "acee8e07",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
